id: pm-f38ovr
title: Recognize literal dynamic imports in module-usage evidence
description: The orphan-module check inspects only top-level import/export declarations while the SDK boundary parser already resolves literal dynamic imports. Optional lazy merge helpers are falsely rejected as orphan modules. Reuse the existing AST parser without allowances or eager imports.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:ci","area:sdk",performance,regression
created_at: "2026-10-18T15:15:30.124Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T16:52:22.870Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T16:52:22.004Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T16:52:22.004Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Prove a nested literal dynamic import fails before the fix; Reuse the existing parser in a recursive AST traversal; Retain unused and computed-only orphan controls without allowance or threshold growth; Pass static-quality regressions and the complete repository static gate
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep optional SDK capabilities lazy while module-usage evidence remains trustworthy
value: Recursive improvement can add optimized primitives without dummy eager imports or weakened release gates
why_now: The merge settlement delivery exposed two false orphan findings when optional helpers were made lazy to preserve SDK import budgets
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Reused the existing module-specifier AST parser in a recursive module-usage walk. Nested literal lazy imports now count as usage while computed-only, comment-only and unused targets remain orphan findings. Removed one obsolete ESLint suppression and lowered both source and registered provider ceilings to104."
expected_result: "Support lazy optional SDK primitives without dummy eager imports, module allowances, threshold growth or inconsistent import parsing."
actual_result: "The extended orphan fixture failed before the fix; all68 static-quality cases, all25 release-automation cases and the gate-registry inventory now pass. The full static pipeline passed; real scans report zero orphans and no changed-file complexity violation. Both original and candidate import-cost checks pass without budget growth, and all linked tests were rerun."
